NEXT ACTION: [0m COMMAND = express_hypothesis  ARGUMENTS = {'hypothesis': 'In src/libcrun/seccomp.c, get_seccomp_action parses OCI seccomp action strings by stripping the SCMP_ACT_ prefix and matching a fixed set of suffixes. The function supports ALLOW, ERRNO, KILL, TRAP, TRACE, and conditionally KILL_PROCESS, but it does not recognize LOG. Therefore a valid OCI config using defaultAction "SCMP_ACT_LOG" falls through to the fail path and reports an invalid seccomp action instead of returning libseccomp\'s SCMP_ACT_LOG value. The repair should add a compile-time guarded LOG case (e.g. #ifdef SCMP_ACT_LOG) returning SCMP_ACT_LOG near the other simple actions, preserving builds against older libseccomp headers while enabling runtimes built with LOG support to accept and apply the action.'}
